
=== a declared batch changes the cost, not the answer
the two paths agree: ok
an absent key answers None: ok
with no native batch, a key is a read: ok
with one, the whole run is a request: ok

=== a run is bounded by count and by bytes
300 keys is two requests, not one: ok
and so is 12 MB of bodies: ok

=== a refused batch is asked key by key; a lost one is not
a store's refusal costs a read per key: ok
a link's loss reaches the caller, with no key asked: ok

=== a pool bounds the reads a batch makes at once
  3 read(s) at once under a pool of three
no more run at once than the pool admits: ok
and the bound is what capped it: ok
  16 read(s) at once under a pool of sixteen
a wider pool runs more of them at once: ok

